atcit><patcit ucid="JP-9120090-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9120090</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9179152-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9179152</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9331297-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9331297</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1018666A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKASAKA YOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EMORI YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA ELECTRIC CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI SHU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKASAKA, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EMORI, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI, SHU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>THE FURUKAWA ELECTRIC CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKASAKA YOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>EMORI YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI SHU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKASAKA, YOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EMORI, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI, SHU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A Raman amplifier comprises a pumping light producing means (1) for producing pumping lights.  The pumping lights are multiplexed with a signal light propagated through an optical fiber (2) so as to give the signal light a Raman gain. The means (1) is constituted of a semiconductor laser of Fabri-Perot, DFB, or DBR type and an MOPA (3). The center wavelengths of the pumping lights are different from each other, and the intervals between them are 6 nm to 35 nm.  An optical repeater provided in an optical fiber transmission line (8) compensates the loss caused by the optical fiber transmission line (8) and includes the Raman amplifier (9) used for the compensation. A Raman amplification method for Raman-amplifying a signal light by sending the signal light and pumping lights having mutually different center wavelengths through an optical fiber serving as a Raman-amplification medium, in which the power of the pumping light having a shorter wavelength is higher.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un amplificateur Raman, comprenant des moyens de production (1) de lumières de pompage. Ces lumières de pompage sont multiplexées avec un signal optique propagé à travers une fibre optique (2), afin de donner un gain Raman à ce signal optique. Les moyens de production (1) de lumières de pompage sont constitués d'un laser de Fabri-Perot semi-conducteur de type DFB ou DBR et d'un MOPA (3). Les longueurs d'onde centrales des lumières de pompage sont différentes les unes des autres, et les intervalles entre chacune d'elles vont de 6 nm à 35 nm. Un répéteur optique, placé dans une ligne de transmission (8) à fibre optique, compense la perte provoquée par cette ligne de transmission (8) à fibre optique, et comprend l'amplificateur Raman utilisé pour la compensation. L'invention concerne également un procédé d'amplification Raman permettant une amplification Raman d'un signal optique par envoi de ce signal et des lumières de pompage présentant des longueurs d'onde centrales différentes, à travers une fibre optique servant de support d'amplification Raman, où la puissance de la lumière de pompage possédant une longueur d'onde plus courte, est plus élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>